{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: Grammar-guided node reduction (Perses-style)\n\nThe goal is to implement `solve(case)` that performs a parse tree reduction:\n\n1. Consider nodes from deepest to shallowest (deeper nodes first)\n2. At equal depth, use node ID as stable tie-break\n3. Never remove: root, a required symbol node, or a node with retained children\n4. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented after removal\n5. Return `retained_node_ids` (sorted) and `removed_node_ids` (in actual removal order)\n\nLet me trace through the algorithm:\n\nFor case b-000:\n- nodes: root(depth=0, removable=false), n1(depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1), n2(depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2), n3(depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0), n4(depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2), n5(depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3), n6(depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1)\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcessing order: deeper first, then by node ID for ties.\n- Depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by ID: n4, n5, n6)\n- Depth 1: n1, n2, n3 (sorted by ID: n1, n2, n3)\n- Depth 0: root\n\nLet me process each:\n\nInitially all nodes are \"retained\". \nSymbol coverage: root(root), n1(s1), n2(s2), n3(s0), n4(s1), n5(s2), n6(s0)\nRequired symbols: root, s1\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2):\n- Check: removable=true ✓\n- Check: n4 has no children, so no retained children to worry about ✓\n- Check: if we remove n4, remaining symbols = {root(root), n1(s1), n2(s2), n3(s0), n5(s2), n6(s0)}\n  - required \"root\" covered by root ✓\n  - required \"s1\" covered by n1 ✓\n- Remove n4. removal_order = [n4]\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, removable=false):\n- removable=false → skip\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1):\n- removable=true ✓\n- No children ✓\n- If removed: remaining = {root, n1(s1), n2(s2), n3(s0), n5(s2)}\n  - required symbols: root ✓, s1 (covered by n1) ✓\n- Remove n6. removal_order = [n4, n6]\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- removable=false → skip\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2):\n- removable=true ✓\n- Children of n2: n4 (already removed) → no retained children ✓\n- If removed: remaining = {root, n1(s1), n3(s0), n5(s2)}\n  - required symbols: root ✓, s1 (covered by n1) ✓\n- Remove n2. removal_order = [n4, n6, n2]\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- removable=false → skip\n\nProcess root (depth=0, removable=false):\n- removable=false → skip\n\nFinal:\n- removed: [n4, n6, n2]\n- retained: [root, n1, n3, n5] (sorted)\n\nLet me now write the Python implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    import copy\n    \n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing field {field} in node\")\n    \n    # Build a map of node id -\u003e node info\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            parent_id = n[\"parent\"]\n            if parent_id not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {parent_id} not found\")\n            children[parent_id].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track which nodes are currently retained\n    retained = {n[\"id\"] for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Track removal order\n    removal_order = []\n    \n    # Sort nodes: deeper first, then by node ID (stable tie-break)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if already removed (shouldn't happen but just in case)\n        if nid not in retained:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check if node has any retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c in retained for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: check if all required symbols still covered\n        # Current retained symbols excluding this node\n        remaining_retained = retained - {nid}\n        remaining_symbols = {node_map[rid][\"symbol\"] for rid in remaining_retained}\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(remaining_symbols):\n            retained.remove(nid)\n            removal_order.append(nid)\n    \n    # retained_node_ids sorted\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nLet me verify with the test cases.\n\nCase b-000:\nNodes sorted by (-depth, id):\n- depth=2: n4, n5, n6\n- depth=1: n1, n2, n3\n- depth=0: root\n\nInitially retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6}\n\nn4: removable=true, no retained children, symbols after removal = {root, s1(n1), s2(n2), s0(n3), s2(n5), s0(n6)} = {root, s1, s2, s0}. Required {root, s1} ⊆ these → remove n4. retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n5, n6}, removal = [n4]\n\nn5: removable=false → skip\n\nn6: removable=true, no retained children (n6 has no children), symbols after removal = {root(root), s1(n1), s2(n2), s0(n3), s2(n5)} = {root, s1, s2, s0}. Required {root, s1} ⊆ these → remove n6. retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n5}, removal = [n4, n6]\n\nn1: removable=false → skip\n\nn2: removable=true. Children of n2: n4 (already removed, not in retained). No retained children. Symbols after removal = {root(root), s1(n1), s0(n3), s2(n5)} = {root, s1, s0, s2}. Required {root, s1} ⊆ these → remove n2. retained = {root, n1, n3, n5}, removal = [n4, n6, n2]\n\nn3: removable=false → skip\n\nroot: removable=false → skip\n\nFinal: retained_sorted = [n1, n3, n5, root], removal = [n4, n6, n2]\n\nWait, sorting strings: \"n1\" \u003c \"n3\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"root\" — yes that's correct alphabetically.\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me now format it as the required JSON output.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        for field in [\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"]:\\n            if field not in node:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required field '{field}' in node {node.get('id', '?')}\\\")\\n\\n    # Build id -\u003e node map\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n\\n    # Build children map\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            parent_id = n[\\\"parent\\\"]\\n            if parent_id not in node_map:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Parent '{parent_id}' not found for node '{n['id']}'\\\")\\n            children[parent_id].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Track retained set and removal order\\n    retained = {n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes}\\n    removal_order = []\\n\\n    # Process deeper nodes first; stable tie-break by node ID (lexicographic)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Already removed (shouldn't happen, but guard)\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Cannot remove if any child is still retained\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentative removal: check required symbols still covered\\n        remaining = retained - {nid}\\n        covered = {node_map[rid][\\\"symbol\\\"] for rid in remaining}\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(covered):\\n            retained.remove(nid)\\n            removal_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removal_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01JzKiv6tS6CfIzKI9DJomqe","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2559},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2559,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":33,"output_tokens":2543,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1981},"service_tier":"standard"}}